///1GENCMD
Help by Willem Aandewiel
GENCMD - Create an executable CP/M-86 CMD file

GENCMD converts .H86 hexadecimal records into a .CMD load file.
It does not assemble source code.

///2SYNTAX
  A>GENCMD HELP

Reads HELP.H86 and writes HELP.CMD.
Do not add .A86 to this command.
With GENCMD on A: and HELP.H86 on B:, use:

  B>A:GENCMD HELP

///2WORKFLOW
For the supplied HELP program:

  A>ASM86 HELP
  A>GENCMD HELP
  A>HELP

Correct assembler errors before generating or running HELP.CMD.

///2MODELS
GENCMD can describe code, data, stack and extra memory groups.
ASM86 normally supplies the segment information it needs.
The supplied HELP.A86 uses separate code and data groups.
Use GENCMD HELP without an 8080 option for this source.

The 8080 keyword selects a memory layout; it does not convert
8080 instructions or a CP/M-80 .COM program into 8086 code.

///2OPTIONS
Advanced parameters include CODE, DATA, STACK and EXTRA.
Their values control placement and memory allocation.
Use the CP/M-86 System Guide for these parameters; they must
match the program's actual memory layout.

///2CHECKING
After generation, check that HELP.CMD exists:

  A>DIR HELP.CMD

A CMD file can exist even when its input came from faulty source.
Reassemble and regenerate after changing the source.
